{"id": "EUVD-2026-26505", "enisaUuid": "4121e48b-bbea-3286-a0f7-cdb5883eae25", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrxrpc: Fix missing validation of ticket length in non-XDR key preparsing\n\nIn rxrpc_preparse(), there are two paths for parsing key payloads: the\nXDR path (for large payloads) and the non-XDR path (for payloads <= 28\nbytes). While the XDR path (rxrpc_preparse_xdr_rxkad()) correctly\nvalidates the ticket length against AFSTOKEN_RK_TIX_MAX, the non-XDR\npath fails to do so.\n\nThis allows an unprivileged user to provide a very large ticket length.\nWhen this key is later read via rxrpc_read(), the total\ntoken size (toksize) calculation results in a value that exceeds\nAFSTOKEN_LENGTH_MAX, triggering a WARN_ON().\n\n[ 2001.302904] WARNING: CPU: 2 PID: 2108 at net/rxrpc/key.c:778 rxrpc_read+0x109/0x5c0 [rxrpc]\n\nFix this by adding a check in the non-XDR parsing path of rxrpc_preparse()\nto ensure the ticket length does not exceed AFSTOKEN_RK_TIX_MAX,\nbringing it into parity with the XDR parsing logic.", "datePublished": "2026-05-01T13:55:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:17:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/44714dfda386884919ba366411880b6fb3c3efd3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/41a117dd80371343babc52198d1114e83eb37627", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a397aa9b5e53ca63d4d6aefb542832eca389618", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1fa36cf495b0023e8475d038535c05e4063211e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4458757c020592a3094366e0fb20457383b42f92", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce383ba615339f8eaec646a166d2c2b015bb5ca0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1be1c9ece26cea69654f28b255ff9a7906b897b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac33733b10b484d666f97688561670afd5861383"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-31696", "GHSA-jrvq-m3v6-8wm9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2e44acbf-4b1f-34a9-861e-c3d0b56ba806", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a7a3eb4ddbe7c7e639170a64adede7cbd5a9247 <1fa36cf495b0023e8475d038535c05e4063211e1"}, {"id": "341768d8-9cdb-3a7c-9b4c-f7b6ebd10e96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "3d419528-b04a-3ecd-b935-dfc358e4b2bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.17"}, {"id": "4b97584f-8f6f-32ea-a0e6-f03147bd9bfa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.84"}, {"id": "6257dfb2-c9f6-3f7c-9a4f-b62cd996ba12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a7a3eb4ddbe7c7e639170a64adede7cbd5a9247 <41a117dd80371343babc52198d1114e83eb37627"}, {"id": "660116ed-6494-3177-9986-65dc3bdf1276", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6c43cef7-8ed3-3abe-acf8-4e16ffcb99f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.25"}, {"id": "71de72fe-0c29-3074-bcbc-85b3acea7094", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a7a3eb4ddbe7c7e639170a64adede7cbd5a9247 <a1be1c9ece26cea69654f28b255ff9a7906b897b"}, {"id": "9492018c-7538-30bd-a3c8-cbcdbb46fd21", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.258"}, {"id": "a2ebdd40-4c31-3d6d-b052-e9c452585ec5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.136"}, {"id": "ae7a2300-c04c-3fcf-8fce-762f541c4e60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.2"}, {"id": "b46ff788-de6d-30ff-beff-e2b1b0eab76d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a7a3eb4ddbe7c7e639170a64adede7cbd5a9247 <4458757c020592a3094366e0fb20457383b42f92"}, {"id": "b6e8a3c7-31bf-36f2-b365-60ff1791d6b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "p